WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:08.270 position:63%
It's estimated that over 8 million trees
are chopped down every year to make

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:11.870 position:63%
pencils.
Now this company is making them from old

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:15.780 position:58%
newspapers, reducing deforestation in
the process.

00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:21.860 position:98% line:92%
We are suffering from climate action and the best way is to reduce the number

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:27.380 position:64%
of trees that are cut for any purpose.
We want each and every child in Kenya who

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:31.550 position:61%
goes to school to use our pencil and at
the same time be able to plant a tree

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:35.270 position:69%
through our pencil. That way, we will reduce
the number of trees cut.

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:39.140 position:61%
We'll also provide an option and reduce
the number of wooden pencils in the

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.160
market.
This is how they're made. After

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:48.020 position:59%
newspapers are cut to size,
graphite is glued to the paper. That's

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:51.110 position:59%
put into a roller and dried out in the
sun.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:56.090 position:59%
Finally, they're put through a
compressor, sharpened and packaged up.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:01.810 position:61%
We can address climate change by making
pencil from recycled paper. One,

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:05.570 position:97% line:92%
we reduce the amount of trees cut down when we use recycled paper.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:09.590 position:56%
Number two, we reduce the amount of
waste paper that is dumped or burnt.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:12.710 position:75% line:92%
That way, green pencils made from recycled paper

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:14.540 position:58%
contribute also to addressing climate
change.

